  "job_B1.5.2_20251001_193246": {
    "text": "SECUNDUM IOHANNEM Preteriens Iesus uidit hominem cecum a natiuitate & Reliqua VRe drihten,\n\u00dea befrynnon his apostoli hine & cw\u00e6don, For hw\u00e6s synn\u00e6 w\u00e6s \u00f0\u00e6s mon swa blind acenned, hw\u00e6\u00f0er\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0e H\u00e6lend heom son\u00e6 to andsware, N\u00e6s he blind acenned for his agene synnum, o\u00f0\u00f0e for his\nMe idafen\u00e6\u00f0 to wyrcenne his weorc \u00fee me sende \u00fea hwile \u00f0e d\u00e6g bi\u00f0; for\u00f0an \u00fee \u00f0eo deorce niht\nIc am middaneardes liht, \u00fea hwile \u00f0e ic on middanearde \u00e6m.\nMid \u00feam \u00f0e he \u00f0is gecw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fea sp\u00e6tte he on \u00fea eor\u00f0an, & makede of \u00f0am spattle & of \u00f0are eor\u00f0e lam;\nHe eode \u00fea son\u00e6 & his eagan a\u00fewoh, & com agean lokinde.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6don his neahgebur\u00e6s, La.\nHu n\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fee blinde mon \u00fee swa iboren w\u00e6s, \u00fee we iseagen sitt\u00e6n simle w\u00e6dliende?\nSume men \u00fea s\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t hit \u00f0e ylc\u00e6 were, & sume s\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t hit w\u00e6re sum o\u00f0er him ilic; ac he him\nHeo \u00fea axoden him, Humet\u00e6 isixst \u00feu nu?\nHe heom andswyrde & cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00f0e \u00fee is ihaten H\u00e6lend \u00fee wrohte lam of eor\u00f0an, & mine eagen smirode;\nIc eode & weosc me; & ic son\u00e6 iseah.\nHeo axodon him \u00f0a, & hw\u00e6r is he nu?\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he nuste; & heo l\u00e6ddon hine son\u00e6 to \u00feam synderhalgan, for \u00feam sellice wundr\u00e6.\n& \u00fee mon w\u00e6s ih\u00e6led on \u00feam halgan r\u00e6stend\u00e6ge.\n\u00dea axodon \u00fea synderhalgan eft hu he isege.\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0a to \u00feam unleaffullum, Mid lame he me smirode ofer mine eahring\u00e6s, & ic weosc a\u00fewoh me\n\u00dea s\u00e6don sona sume \u00fea synderhalgan, Nis \u00fees mon na from Gode, \u00fee \u00feone r\u00e6stend\u00e6g ne healt.\nHeom andswyrdan \u00fea o\u00f0re, Hu m\u00e6g \u00e6nig synful man \u00feas tacn\u00e6 wyrc\u00e6n?\n& \u00fea wear\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r flit betwyx \u00feam synderhalgan.\n& heo sy\u00f0\u00f0an axodon eft \u00feone ih\u00e6lede mon hw\u00e6t he be \u00feam H\u00e6lende s\u00e6de.\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he were sum halig witega.\n\u00dea nolden \u00fea Iudeiscen ilyfan be \u00feam men \u00fe\u00e6t he were blind acenned, ant wyrde ih\u00e6led, ac clypodon\nHis magas s\u00e6don \u00fea, We witan so\u00f0lice \u00fe\u00e6t he ure sunu is, & \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6s blind acenned; ac we nyten\nAxi\u00e6\u00f0 him sylfne; he h\u00e6f\u00f0 \u00fea yld\u00e6 \u00fe\u00e6t he andswyri\u00e6n m\u00e6g.\n\u00deis s\u00e6don \u00fea magas for \u00fean \u00f0e heo heom as\u00e6ton \u00fe\u00e6t heo wyrden iutlagede of \u00f0are gesamnunge.\nFor \u00feam \u00f0e \u00fea Iudeisc\u00e6n on heor\u00e6 dearne \u00feeohte h\u00e6fdon icw\u00e6den, \u00fe\u00e6t swa hwa swa Crist andette\n\u00dea forleton heo \u00fea magas, & to \u00feam men cw\u00e6don, Do wulder Gode; we witan ful geare \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0es mon is\nHe s\u00e6de heom to andswyre, Nat ic gif he synful is; ac ic wat swa \u00feeah \u00fe\u00e6t ic blind w\u00e6s & ic wislice nu\nHeo axodon hine \u00f0a gyt, Ant hu ih\u00e6lde he \u00f0e?\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0e ih\u00e6lede mon heom to andsware \u00feus, Hwene \u00e6r ic eow s\u00e6de; hw\u00e6t sceal hit eow eft\nLa, wylle ge beon his leorningcniht\u00e6s?\nHeo warigedon \u00fea wodlice hine & cw\u00e6don, Beo \u00feu his leorningcniht; we habb\u00e6\u00f0 ure lareow Moysen\nWe witen \u00fe\u00e6t Moyses sp\u00e6c to \u00feone \u00e6lmihtiga Gode, ac we ne cunnon \u00feisne mon ne hwanon he icumen\n\u00d0a andswarede \u00fee ih\u00e6lede mon \u00feam heardheortan & cw\u00e6\u00f0, On \u00f0am is mucel wunder, \u00f0\u00e6t ge nyten\nSo\u00f0lice we witan \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0e so\u00f0fest\u00e6 God \u00fea synfullen ne gehyr\u00f0 to swylcere bene; ac \u00f0e \u00fee his begenga\nFram \u00feissere weorulde anginne ne wear\u00f0 n\u00e6ffre ihyred \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6nig man mihte \u00feone mon geh\u00e6len & his\nButon he fram Gode were, ne mihte he \u00feis don.\n\u00dea andswaredon \u00fea Iudei him \u00feus huxlice & cw\u00e6don, \u00feu eart \u00e6rming al acenned on synum & \u00feu l\u00e6rst\n& heo belucon hine \u00fea wi\u00f0uton.\n\u00d0a ihyrde \u00f0e H\u00e6lend \u00fe\u00e6t heo hine ut adr\u00e6fdon, & he hine \u00fea imette, & him \u00feus to cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00f0u ilyfest on\nAnd he mid ileafan him andswyrde, Laford la, hwylc is he \u00fe\u00e6t ic ilyfe on hine?\n\u00d0e H\u00e6lend him andswyrde, & \u00feu hine \u00e6r is\u00e6ge, & he is \u00f0e ylca \u00f0e \u00fee to sp\u00e6c\u00f0.\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea mid geleafan, Ic ilyfe, Drihten; & he hine \u00f0a astr\u00e6hte to \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes fotum.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0e H\u00e6lend him eft \u00feus to, Ic com hider on dome on \u00f0isne middaneard, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a men geseon \u00fee\n\u00d0is godspel is nu is\u00e6d swytellice on Englisc anfealdum angite, ac we will\u00e6\u00f0 eow s\u00e6cgen \u00fe\u00e6t gastlice\nFor \u00fean \u00f0e Cristes wundr\u00e6 \u00fee he wrohte on \u00feisse life w\u00e6ron so\u00f0lice gefremede & swutelice mid\n\u00d0es fores\u00e6de blinde mon, \u00f0e swa iboren w\u00e6s, tacnode al moncynn on \u00feisse middanearde, \u00fee wear\u00f0\n& \u00feurh \u00f0\u00e6s deofl\u00e6s onde \u00f0e Adam beswac us becom d\u00e6\u00f0 too & eac unrihtwisnesse; & us for icynde\nNu \u00e6lc \u00feare monn\u00e6 \u00fee mismaky his lif, & on fulum leahtr\u00e6n li\u00f0 ungeleaffullice, his mod is ablend\nNe bi\u00f0 \u00f0e mon na ileafful \u00fee on leahtrum wun\u00e6\u00f0.\n\u00deeo unleaffulnesse is \u00feare heort\u00e6 blindnysse, & \u00fee so\u00f0a geleafa onliht \u00feone mon \u00fee m\u00e6g mid his mode\nBe \u00feam cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0e apostol Paulus on sumon his pistol, Fuimus & nos aliquando filii ire sicud & ceteri;\nYrr\u00e6s bearn bi\u00f0 \u00fee ilc\u00e6 \u00f0e Godes yrre h\u00e6f\u00f0, & \u00f0e bi\u00f0 dea\u00f0es bearn \u00fee dea\u00fees wyr\u00f0e bi\u00f0.\nMan cw\u00e6\u00f0 on bocum gehu be \u00feissum bearnteame, \u00fe\u00e6t gehwa beo icw\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6s sun\u00e6 \u00fee he folg\u00e6\u00f0\nEft he bi\u00f0 wracane sun\u00e6 \u00fee \u00f0e wr\u00e6c\u00e6 iearn\u00e6\u00f0; & he bi\u00f0 helle sunu, \u00fee \u00f0e helle geearn\u00e6\u00f0.\nNu alle \u00f0eos yfelnesse w\u00e6s on us wunigende \u00e6r \u00feam \u00f0e \u00fee mildheort\u00e6 Crist, \u00fee is middaneardes liht,\n& \u00f0a \u00f0e on hine gelyf\u00e6\u00f0 he mid his so\u00f0an geleafan so\u00f0lice onlihte; & \u00fea \u00f0e ne gelyf\u00e6\u00f0 libb\u00e6\u00f0 on\nHw\u00e6t dyde \u00fee H\u00e6lend \u00fea \u00f0a he h\u00e6lde \u00feonne blindne?\nHe sp\u00e6tte on \u00fea eor\u00f0an, & of \u00feam spatle macode lam; for \u00fean \u00f0e his godcundnesse underfeng \u00fea\nHe smirode his eagen eac mid \u00feam lame; ac he w\u00e6s \u00feeah swa blind o\u00f0\u00f0et \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6ter hine a\u00f0woh \u00fee is\n\u00d0e H\u00e6lend w\u00e6s asend so\u00f0lice to us to ure alysednesse fram his Almihtig\u00e6 F\u00e6der; & buton he wyrde\n\u00d0enne \u00f0e mon bi\u00f0 icristnod & me him t\u00e6c\u00f0 his ileafan, \u00feonne beo\u00f0 his eagan ismirode; ac he ne isih\u00f0\nHis leorningcniht\u00e6s befrunnon hine & cw\u00e6don, For hw\u00e6s synnum w\u00e6s \u00f0es mon swa blind acenned,\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0a H\u00e6lend heom son\u00e6 to andsware, N\u00e6s he blind acenned for his agene synnum, o\u00f0\u00f0e for\nNes \u00f0e blind\u00e6 man swa \u00feeah buton synnum on life, for\u00fean \u00f0e monig blind mon bi\u00f0 swi\u00f0e manful, ac\nMe gedafen\u00e6\u00f0 to wyrcenne his weorc \u00f0e me asende.\nNu ge magen ihyren hu \u00f0e H\u00e6lend wear\u00f0 asend fram his Almihtiga Fader, swa swa we \u00e6r cw\u00e6don.\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t him gedafenode to wyrccenne his weorc for \u00feam \u00f0e he is his Sunu of \u00feam so\u00f0an F\u00e6der,\nFor\u00fean \u00f0e he of him is al \u00fe\u00e6t he is, eafre acenned Sunu unasegenlice; & \u00fee F\u00e6der nis na of nanum\nCrist cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fea hwile \u00fee hit d\u00e6g bi\u00f0, for \u00feam \u00f0e \u00feeo deorce niht cym\u00f0, \u00feonne nan mon ne m\u00e6g noht\nHwilc is \u00f0e d\u00e6g, o\u00f0\u00f0e hw\u00e6t is \u00feeo niht?\nCrist cw\u00e6\u00f0 him sylf \u00fe\u00e6t he is \u00f0eo so\u00f0e liht \u00feisses middaneardes, & he is ure d\u00e6g, \u00f0e us mid geileaf\u00e6n\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ic eam middaneardes liht, \u00fea hwile \u00f0e \u00fee ic on middanearde \u00e6m.\nHw\u00e6t wene we la, bro\u00f0r\u00e6, \u00fe\u00e6t he were \u00fea mid monnum, \u00fea \u00fea he on menniscnesse on middanearde\nNis hit na swa \u00feeah swa we on \u00f0are swarte nihte ure lif adreogon buton Cristes lihte.\nHis apostoli wrohten fela wyndr\u00e6 & tacn\u00e6 \u00e6fter his upstige, & eac heom becom to \u00f0e Halige Gast of\nHeo wrohten eac \u00fea wundr\u00e6 \u00fee Crist sylf ne wrohte; for \u00fean \u00fee he s\u00e6de to heom \u00e6r his \u00f0rowunge,\nSwa \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a leaffulle men l\u00e6dden \u00f0a untruman men on heor\u00e6 l\u00e6gerbeddum, & l\u00e6gdon heom bi \u00feere\nNe h\u00e6lde \u00fee H\u00e6lend nenne mon \u00feurh his sc\u00e6de, ac \u00feeos miht com of him swa \u00feeah; for\u00fean \u00f0e he\n\u00dees weoruldlice d\u00e6g \u00fee us gewunelic is, bi\u00f0 iendod mid \u00fean onsigendum \u00e6fne; ac \u00fee drihtenlic\u00e6 d\u00e6g,\nSwa swa Crist sylf behet \u00feam \u00f0e hine lufi\u00e6\u00f0, Ecce ego uobiscum sum omnibus diebus usque ad\nHw\u00e6t is \u00f0eo deorce niht buton helledimnes, on \u00fe\u00e6re nan mon ne m\u00e6g naht to gode wyrcean, \u00fee \u00f0e nu\nO\u00f0er is weorces tim\u00e6, o\u00f0er is \u00e6tleanes tim\u00e6.\nNu is weorces tim\u00e6 o\u00f0 \u00feissere weorulde endunge; & \u00e6fter ure life bi\u00f0 eadleanes tim\u00e6, \u00feonne Crist on\n\u00deis is \u00fe\u00e6t edlean \u00feare rihtwis\u00e6 monn\u00e6 \u00fee rihtlice leofedon, & mid gode weorce Gode icw\u00e6mdon.\n\u00d0eo dimme niht bi\u00f0 \u00f0onne ure Drihten clyp\u00e6\u00f0 on \u00feam miclan dome to \u00feam manfull\u00e6 heape \u00fee mid\n\u00deonne underfo\u00f0 heo edlean on ecere \u00feine heor\u00e6 arleas\u00e6 d\u00e6da \u00fee heo \u00e6fre adrugon o\u00f0 heor\u00e6 lifes\nOn \u00f0are nihte cwylmde, swa swa Cristes boc us s\u00e6g\u00f0, \u00fee w\u00e6lga rice; \u00f0e walde \u00fea habban Lazarum\nAc him w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6s w\u00e6tan forwyrnd, swa swa he forwyrnde \u00e6r \u00fea crumen \u00feam earm\u00e6n Lazare.\nHim com \u00fea to gemynde his gebro\u00f0r\u00e6 on life; wolde \u00fea god wyrcan, & heom warnig\u00e6n \u00fe\u00e6t heo \u00f0ider\nAc \u00fea nes na weorces tim\u00e6, ac w\u00e6s edleanes; & he w\u00e6s \u00fea on \u00feare nihte \u00fe\u00e6r he wyrcen ne mihte.\n\u00d0is godspel is langsum & h\u00e6f\u00f0 longne traht.\nNu wylle we eow secgan \u00fe\u00e6t arfo\u00feeste andgit; \u00fe\u00e6t o\u00f0er ge magon eow seolfe understanden.\n\u00d0e mon w\u00e6s ih\u00e6led on \u00feam halga r\u00e6stend\u00e6g.\n\u00dea s\u00e6don son\u00e6 sume \u00fea sunderhalgan, Nis \u00f0es mon na fram Gode, \u00fee \u00f0onne restand\u00e6g ne heald.\n\u00dea Iudeiscan heoldon heom to freolsd\u00e6ge \u00feonne S\u00e6teresd\u00e6g, & na \u00f0one Sunnend\u00e6g, on \u00fea aldan\n\u00d0e S\u00e6teresd\u00e6g \u00fee heo swa swi\u00f0e freolsoden is ure gastlice freols, \u00fee we for Gode sceolon haldan on\nSwa swa Crist seolf cw\u00e6\u00f0 on sumne godspelle, Omnis qui facit peccatum seruus est peccati, \u00e6lc \u00f0are\nIs nu \u00fee r\u00e6stand\u00e6g ure lifes tim\u00e6, on \u00feam we sceolon simle synne forbugon, swa we selost magon,\n\u00dea Iudeiscan freolsoden \u00feone fors\u00e6don r\u00e6stand\u00e6g fram weoruldlice weorcum, ac heo gewemdon swa\nHe heold \u00feonne restand\u00e6g \u00feeah \u00f0e he ih\u00e6lde \u00feonne blindan, for\u00f0an \u00f0e he leofede his lif buton\n& we halgi\u00e6\u00f0 nu him \u00feone halgan sunnand\u00e6g, for\u00fean \u00f0e he on \u00f0am d\u00e6ge of dea\u00fee aras, \u00f0a \u00fee he us\nHeo cw\u00e6don to \u00f0am men, Do wuldor Gode; swylc heo cw\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t Crist n\u00e6re God, & he sceolde\nWe witen ful gear\u00e6 \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6s mon is synful; \u00f0is s\u00e6don \u00fea Iudeiscan be \u00feam so\u00f0fest\u00e6n H\u00e6lende, \u00fee ne\nAc heo weron synfulle, \u00f0eah \u00f0e heo swa ne wendon, & heom w\u00e6re b\u00e6tere \u00fe\u00e6t heo wrohton alle d\u00e6g\n\u00d0e restand\u00e6g wes ihalgod on \u00f0es H\u00e6lendes \u00f0rowunge fram \u00f0eowtlicum weorce; ac we nu \u00f0urfon na\n\u00dea Iudesican warigedon wodlice \u00f0one blindan sy\u00f0\u00f0an he ih\u00e6led w\u00e6s, \u00fea he be \u00feam H\u00e6lende sp\u00e6c &\nHeo s\u00e6don him to andsware, Beo \u00f0u his leorningcniht, swylce he w\u00e6re awariged gif he cristene w\u00e6re.\nAc \u00fe\u00e6t nis na warigung, ac witolice bl\u00e6tsung \u00fe\u00e6t mon Criste folgie mid so\u00f0\u00e6 cristendome.\nHeo temdon to Moysen \u00feam m\u00e6ran lareowe \u00fe\u00e6t heo his leorningcniht\u00e6s weron & his lare folgodon;\n& \u00fea Iudeiscan noldon now\u00fere folgian ne Moysen ne Criste mid nane so\u00f0festnesse.\n\u00d0e ih\u00e6lede mon cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t God nele ihyran \u00fea synfulle men, ac he ne s\u00e6de na riht.\nFor\u00fean \u00f0e he ne cu\u00f0e \u00feagyt \u00fea halga Cristes boc \u00fee s\u00e6\u00f0 hu \u00fee manfulle mid mycele onbrurdnesse\nWe nyton, \u00feeah he mende \u00fe\u00e6t micele wundor, \u00fe\u00e6t nan synful man ne mihte swylce tacn\u00e6 wyrc\u00e6n.\n\u00d0e ih\u00e6lede mon cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00feam heardheortum Iudeiscum, Fram \u00feissere weorlde anginne ne wear\u00f0\nFreolice he sp\u00e6c her, & ful andr\u00e6dlice, Hwa mihte openigan \u00fea unsceapen\u00e6 eagen & him sih\u00f0e gifen,\n\u00d0a yrsodan \u00fea Iudeiscan & hine utdrifon.\nAc Crist hine underfeng \u00fea \u00fea heo hine fors\u00e6gen & him son\u00e6 cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, \u00feu ilefest on Godes Sunu?\nHe andswyrde mid ileafan, La hwylc is he, laford, \u00fe\u00e6t ic ilefe on hine ?\n& \u00fee H\u00e6lend cw\u00e6\u00f0 him to, \u00feu hine is\u00e6ge \u00e6r, & he is \u00f0e ilc\u00e6 \u00fee \u00fee to sp\u00e6ky.\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea mid ileafan, Ic ilyfe, Drihten, & feol to his fotum; for\u00fean \u00f0e he oncneow \u00f0et hit idafenlice\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0e H\u00e6lend him eft to \u00feus, Ic com hider on dome on \u00feisne middaneard, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a men iseon \u00fee\n\u00dees mon w\u00e6s blind iboren, ac he iseah \u00feurh Criste \u00e6g\u00f0er mid eagan & mid geleafan.\n\u00dea Iudeiscan wendon \u00fe\u00e6t heo weron hale, ac heo ne isegon na Crist mid so\u00f0\u00e6 leaf\u00e6, ne his lihtes ne\nHeo hine isegen swutelice mid eagan, & mid hearde heort\u00e6 huxlice forsegon.\nWe hine ne isegon mid lichamlicere gesih\u00f0e, ac we hine iseo\u00f0 nu mid so\u00f0\u00e6 geleafan.\nHeo \u00feurhwunedon on blindnesse, & we wurdon onlihte \u00f0urh \u00f0one lyfigendan Drihten \u00fee leof\u00e6\u00f0 a on\nAMEN.",
